Dear Dr. Nambiar,

Thank you for the referral query. The ALT/AST pattern you describe
(hepatocellular, 4.7× ULN) is certainly concerning and warrants prompt
investigation.

For a 47-year-old male with this pattern, my suggested initial workup
would include:

1. Full viral hepatitis serology: HBsAg, anti-HCV, anti-HBc (total and IgM)
2. Autoimmune markers: ANA, ASMA, LKM-1, AMA
3. Metabolic markers: fasting lipids, fasting insulin, BMI, waist circumference
4. Drug history: thorough medication reconciliation including OTC, supplements,
   herbal products, and any medications prescribed by other specialists.
   DILI (drug-induced liver injury) must be on the differential given the
   5-year progressive rise without prior hepatic diagnosis.
5. If viral and autoimmune excluded: consider liver biopsy assessment.

I note the insurance pre-authorisation issue. Our standard requirement is
that hepatitis serology and a complete drug history disclosure form must
be submitted prior to the referral appointment.

Happy to see the patient urgently once those are in hand.

Kind regards,
Dr. Leontine Voss
Consultant Hepatologist
Merton Hepatology Centre

